            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did pukai mean, and what did kaṉal mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: பசு",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பசு (pasu) — \"a cow\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The animal a Tamil household is built around. Kannada says ಹಸು (hasu): the same word, with the p-for-h trade Kannada makes right through its old words — the one this book pointed out when the numbers were lined up side by side. Tamil keeps the p."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It belongs to a விவசாயி before it belongs to anybody, and in a கிராமம் it stands tied in the yard rather than shut in a shed, near enough to the வாசல் that you step around it going in."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five animals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pasu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pasu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pasu, then kirāmam, and put the one inside the other",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pasu*, then *kirāmam*, and put the one inside the other]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
