          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ஆடு",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஆடு (āṭu) — \"a goat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Smaller, cheaper, and kept by houses with no land for a பசு (pasu). It eats what it finds and needs nobody to cut for it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Start it long — ஆ, held — and put the ட of கூடை in the middle. That keeps it clear of அது, which starts short and is a different word entirely. Kannada parts company here and says ಮೇಕೆ (mēke)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
