          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: கோழி",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கோழி (kōḻi) — \"a hen\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hen or cock alike; the word does not split them, and where the difference matters a second word goes in front. Kannada ಕೋಳಿ (kōḷi) and Telugu కోడి (kōḍi) are the same word three ways, and the middle letter is where they separate: Tamil's ழ, Kannada's ಳ, Telugu's డ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is the clock of a கிராமம். A கோழி (kōḻi) has a house awake well before anybody there needs to know the மணி."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
