          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "காக்கை (kākkai) — \"a crow\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Named off the noise it makes, and the sisters landed on the same trick from the same starting point: Kannada ಕಾಗೆ (kāge). Say it once and you have the etymology."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Of everything with wings around a Tamil house this is the one the house deals with daily. சாதம் set out on the வாசல் step is put there for the காக்கை (kākkai), and it comes down within the minute."
            }
          ]
        },
