          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பறவை (paṟavai) — \"a bird\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The wide word. Whatever flies is a பறவை (paṟavai), the கோழி (kōḻi) and the காக்கை (kākkai) taken in along with everything that was never given a name of its own."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Here the three go three ways: Kannada ಹಕ್ಕಿ (hakki), Telugu పక్షి (pakṣi) off the Sanskrit, and Tamil's own பறவை (paṟavai). The ற in the middle is the hard one, the same ற standing in ஆறு."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and the run is closed: a cow, a goat, a hen, a crow, and the word for everything that flies."
            }
          ]
        },
